      "timestamp": "2026-09-26T06:56:46.073Z",
      "message": "Holding before the edit — this one line is a security-posture change, not just a value.\n\n`SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30` → `480` extends how long an authenticated session stays valid by 16x. The consequence: a stolen session token (shared/unlocked machine, XSS, leaked cookie) stays usable for a full workday instead of half an hour, and an idle session on an unattended device stays logged in all day. `server.js:2` confirms this value is what governs session expiry, so nothing else moderates it.\n\nConfirm and I'll make the change — it's a one-line edit to `config.js:3`.\n\nWorth knowing if you'd rather adjust the shape of the request: an 8-hour *idle* timeout is the risky part. If the goal is \"users stop getting logged out mid-task,\" a sliding/refresh window with a shorter idle timeout gets that without the long-lived-token exposure. Say the word and I'll just do the straight bump.",
